        "audio_url": "https://dcs-spotify.megaphone.fm/NSR9658870995.mp3?key=629b1328c45c991bad4df8f376ed35c6&request_event_id=2f7068c0-f876-4bd7-a7a3-3150159ab27d&session_id=2f7068c0-f876-4bd7-a7a3-3150159ab27d&timetoken=1795305250_ED95158F2FA39A5E9643B1CB04DD84B9",
        "description": "At just ten years old, Juan Carlos was handed over to General Franco as a hostage – the price his father paid to keep their family's claim to the Spanish throne alive. It was the start of an apprenticeship designed to produce Franco's ideal successor: a king who would keep the dictatorship's ideals alive long after its architect was gone. However, as Paul Preston tells Danny Bird, Juan Carlos would go on to confound expectations by overseeing Spain’s transition to democracy – only to face disgrace in more recent years. ----- GO BEYOND THE PODCAST Explore the history of Spain before the reign of Juan Carlos in this episode on Franco: https://bit.ly/4bc61UL ----- GET MORE WITH MEMBERSHIP Become a HistoryExtra podcast member and unlock access to The Full Story podcast, plus enjoy ad-free listening, early access to other podcast episodes, and a member-exclusive newsletter. Find out more and sign up here: ⁠https://historyextra.supportingcast.fm⁠ ----- EXPLORE MORE For more fascinating stories from the past, head to HistoryExtra, the home of ‘History’s Greatest’ podcasts. Find out more at ⁠⁠⁠historyextra.com/podcast⁠⁠⁠. ----- GET IN TOUCH We'd love to know what you think about the podcast, so leave us a review and let us know the topics you think we should be covering. Or, follow us on ⁠Facebook⁠, ⁠X⁠, ⁠Instagram⁠ or ⁠YouTube⁠ to keep in touch. Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices",
